## Usage

[% if domain.extras.makefile %]
### With make

```bash
make help                      # lists the available targets
make lint                      # helm lint on every environment
make template ENV=[[ domain.environments[0].name ]][[ " " * (10 - domain.environments[0].name|length) ]]# renders the manifests without applying them
make validate ENV=[[ domain.environments[0].name ]][[ " " * (10 - domain.environments[0].name|length) ]]# renders then validates with kubeconform
make validate-all              # validates every environment
make install ENV=[[ domain.environments[0].name ]][[ " " * (11 - domain.environments[0].name|length) ]]# deploys on the chosen environment
```

### Raw helm commands
[% else %]
### helm commands
[% endif %]

[% for env in domain.environments %]
Environment `[[ env.name ]]`:

```bash
# Local rendering, with no contact with the cluster
helm template [[ service.name ]] ./charts/[[ service.name ]] \
  --namespace [[ env.namespace ]] \
  --values ./charts/[[ service.name ]]/values.yaml \
  --values ./charts/[[ service.name ]]/values-[[ env.name ]].yaml

# Deployment
helm upgrade --install [[ service.name ]] ./charts/[[ service.name ]] \
  --namespace [[ env.namespace ]] --create-namespace \
  --values ./charts/[[ service.name ]]/values.yaml \
  --values ./charts/[[ service.name ]]/values-[[ env.name ]].yaml \
  --wait --timeout 5m
```

[% endfor %]
## Validation

A rendered manifest must always pass the three following checks before reaching a
cluster:

```bash
# 1. Consistency of the chart
helm lint ./charts/[[ service.name ]]

# 2. Effective rendering of each environment
[% for env in domain.environments %]
helm template [[ service.name ]] ./charts/[[ service.name ]] \
  --values ./charts/[[ service.name ]]/values-[[ env.name ]].yaml > /dev/null
[% endfor %]

# 3. Conformance to the schemas of the Kubernetes [[ domain.kubernetes.version ]] API
helm template [[ service.name ]] ./charts/[[ service.name ]] | \
  kubeconform -strict -summary -kubernetes-version [[ domain.kubernetes.full_version ]] -
```

## Modifying the project

Two paths, according to the nature of the change:

1. **Structural change** (adding a component, an environment, a resource kind):
   modify `forge.yml` then run `forge generate --only helm --force` again — or
   `forge update --only helm`, which applies the evolutions of the template
   **without** overwriting your modifications.
2. **Operational tuning** (replicas, resources, hosts): modify
   `charts/[[ service.name ]]/values-<env>.yaml` directly.

Careful: a regeneration rewrites the files of the chart. The modifications made
by hand in `templates/` will be lost; carry them over into `forge.yml`.

## Tree

The `forge.yml` specification lives at the **root of the repository**, one level
above: it describes the whole service, not only its chart. What follows is the
content of `helm/`.

```
.
[% if domain.extras.makefile %]
├── Makefile                        # lint / template / validate / install shortcuts
[% endif %]
└── charts/[[ service.name ]]/
    ├── Chart.yaml                  # metadata of the chart
    ├── values.yaml                 # default values, entirely commented
[% for env in domain.environments %]
    ├── values-[[ env.name ]].yaml[[ " " * (18 - env.name|length) ]]# divergences of the [[ env.name ]] environment
[% endfor %]
    ├── README.md                   # documentation of the chart and of its values
    └── templates/                  # templates of the Kubernetes resources
```
